ns **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82de10f4-7332-5626-90a4-f9d07ab8004e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313392} {:answer/id #uuid "5c997e41-256f-5693-8c8c-873605a59969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313393} {:answer/id #uuid "5106b55d-32ee-5514-8cf2-a52a48a41c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313394} {:answer/id #uuid "7008c4e3-5378-5b0a-8dfa-b4b53c63473a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313395} {:answer/id #uuid "7c725d1b-95d5-58ab-98ef-b45a25567ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c725d1b-95d5-58ab-98ef-b45a25567ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313396} :answer-field/id #uuid "076a2bf4-6dd3-5693-9b25-85605cb2191f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radi