ts of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "173d05e7-01f8-51b4-a99e-999eb2297643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313413} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dbffa8-6113-59da-ad39-c2488257d668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca1441d-a1bb-5fac-a85c-a812b4552a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313415} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2fa85d-6a95-50ac-97d9-aec3ea556a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313416} {:answer/id #uuid "bda3ac34-c1f5-5c5b-9aa0-f0172157000f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bda3ac34-c1f5-5c5b-9aa0-f0172157000f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313417} :answer-field/id #uuid "73e57294-2bc2-5a6a-baf6-938fa2d12d95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4797a5fc-2e5a-5543-a7ef-ee02e800dc29" :question/math-academy-id "q-71791" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$\n- $[-1,1]$\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-1,1]$ is closed. The boundary points are $-1$, and $1.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$ has a boundary point $0$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d86aaa2c-582e-5c4e-a171-52dc60a49978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313420} {:answer/id #uuid "70f05e09-f360-5406-b3bc-b61aff489e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313421} {:answer/id #uuid "bdeaeec0-fa9c-5a66-b376-2faa02c1c697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313422} {:answer/id #uuid "d6dcaa9c-2bae-51dc-814f-1d825bfb648b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313423} {:answer/id #uuid "68fd36d7-ec93-54be-a925-19fced43c218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdeaeec0-fa9c-5a66-b376-2faa02c1c697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313422} :answer-field/id #uuid "3200f8d9-f792-5d1b-923d-9d1df4c6b4fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c7665c1-52d6-545f-ac10-98880196af2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71798" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- $(-\\infty ,-2)$\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-\\infty ,-2)$ is open. The boundary point of the set is $-2$ and it does not lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $2$, $7$, and $9$, and the points $2$, $7$, and $9$ lies in the set.\n\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$ has four boundary points $-5$, $-1$, $2$, and $4$, and the points $-5$ and $-1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc242303-55c6-5087-b6bb-3c37841fa519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313427} {:answer/id #uuid "00528e60-ed33-5124-a712-3fc52ce3013c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313428} {:answer/id #uuid "05b22d51-c74e-5f14-9f29-36f41d10547e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313429} {:answer/id #uuid "39caf4b2-4d44-51b6-a917-ec27da388cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313430} {:answer/id #uuid "25ed72aa-7b64-581a-80af-b9f80779bdb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39caf4b2-4d44-51b6-a917-ec27da388cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313430} :answer-field/id #uuid "7538b2bf-3286-5310-9935-b39098b90123" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f6c0d61-9e1d-5ec8-86b0-5397402ddce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71802" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- $[-7,1]$\n- $(-1,3]\\cup [4,5)$\n- $(-5,-1)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-5,-1)$ is open. The boundary points are $-5$, and $-1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $[-7,1]$ has two boundary points $-7$, and $1$, and both of them lie in the set.\n\n- $(-1,3]\\cup [4,5)$ has four boundary points $-1$, $3$, $4$, and $5$, and the points $3$ and $4$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4272d47-9824-575a-bb74-8370479d7dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192013} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a2ffb1-2994-5af0-a6a8-d27af289740b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192014} {:answer/id #uuid "0696e5b8-f0d9-5442-bf57-d02becae93a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192015} {:answer/id #uuid "35dcc400-0df2-518a-bbb6-b33df3c4954d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192016} {:answer/id #uuid "6382628d-232c-5c06-ba36-4871dc22c12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6382628d-232c-5c06-ba36-4871dc22c12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192017} :answer-field/id #uuid "120898f5-1296-5643-84d0-da42896f2d93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a3b9409-39a3-5316-8079-d83249ab7774" :question/math-academy-id "q-71808" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0<y<{x}^{2},\\,0<x<1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }1\\le x\\le 4,\\,1\\le {y}^{2}\\le 4}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }0\\le x\\le 3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a0e4d4-22a7-5870-b218-fd084174635c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313434} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb81cbb-7c82-5b7d-9019-e7b6e6745daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313435} {:answer/id #uuid "ba642d60-01ad-5d63-a3a9-d8b681bc63ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313436} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc7ec19-73e8-5748-b28f-e974847c909c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313437} {:answer/id #uuid "8e296532-a1c0-5c01-a8aa-9232c7c3f83d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e296532-a1c0-5c01-a8aa-9232c7c3f83d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313438} :answer-field/id #uuid "4164fab3-ae53-5feb-bd4f-3886e8ac80ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "471d1261-e300-57c0-b122-bc7ed711a2cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71815" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2x+y<6,\\,0<x<3}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }1\\le x<3,\\,2<y\\le 4}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}<6}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,4).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *open *since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "635e058d-dad8-552d-8a4a-c548bafbe782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313441} {:answer/id #uuid "385e4778-985d-5e03-9be2-f6e0f9dc9cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313442} {:answer/id #uuid "90fc032f-75d8-5939-8ced-84e69ab270ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313443} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdf5cc6-1487-5ca7-b474-001715203b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313444} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4585da-32e2-5518-bdcf-a999396955e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4585da-32e2-5518-bdcf-a999396955e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a9d081-809c-51a0-b066-87a6237928fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66f09208-ab13-5d7f-978f-9d23f85b647d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71820" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<y\\le 4}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 9}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,4).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
